%description:

The legacy-key guard (RadioMedium::checkForLegacyConfigKeys(), called from
RadioMedium::initialize()) turns a stale ini key -- one OMNeT++ gives no
diagnostic for, because an ini key matching no parameter is silently ignored
-- into a startup error. Checks all four rule classes at once, since the
guard collects every offender before throwing: a removed parameter name
(antennGainMicro), a deleted parameter name (pathLossType),
a stale *value* naming a deleted NED type (Tr38901ChannelModel), and --
armed once no module is named channelModel/nrChannelModel any more --
the path rule: an otherwise-live parameter name (componentCarrierModules)
reached through a path segment naming a module that no longer exists.

%file: test.ned

import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.RadioMedium;

network Test extends RadioMedium
{
}

%inifile: test.ini
[General]
**.antennGainMicro = 5
**.antennGainEnB = 5
**.channelModel[0].pathLossType = "Tr36873"
**.cellularNic.channelModelType = "Tr38901ChannelModel"
**.cellularNic.channelModel.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0]"

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
antennGainMicro

%contains-regex: stderr
antennGainEnB

%contains-regex: stderr
pathLossType

%contains-regex: stderr
Tr38901ChannelModel

%contains-regex: stderr
componentCarrierModules

%contains-regex: stderr
now named "radio"
